    "faq": [
      { "q": "Why does my Knoxville business need a custom-coded website?", "a": "With Knoxville expected to be the #1 'move-to' city in the U.S. by 2026 and hundreds of new businesses launching each year (244 new business licenses in July 2023 alone, up 13%), custom code eliminates WordPress bloat so your site loads instantly. This is crucial when 53% of mobile users abandon sites that take >3 seconds to load, especially in a city with 40,000+ UT students and a young, tech-savvy population that lives on smartphones." },
      { "q": "How can SEO help me stand out as more people move to Knoxville?", "a": "High inbound migration means lots of new residents actively searching for services online. Rising competition for local search due to hundreds of new businesses each year. We build long-term authority via white-hat SEO: structured content, local signals (reviews, local backlinks), accurate NAP + schema, and authoritative Knoxville-focused content. This helps you steadily climb Knoxville's search rankings even against older, established domains." },
      { "q": "Do you work with new Knoxville startups as well as established local businesses?", "a": "Yes. Knox County issued 244 new business licenses in July 2023 alone, up 13% from the previous year. Most new ventures are in services, construction, retail, and finance/real estate. We specialize in building fast, scalable, custom-coded websites that help both startups and established businesses thrive in Knoxville's growing, competitive market." },
      { "q": "Can you help my Knoxville company show up when people search 'near me' on Google?", "a": "Yes. In a city with lots of newcomers, Google Maps / Google Business Profile is crucial. We ensure complete and accurate NAP (Name, Address, Phone), up-to-date hours and categories, quality photos and occasional posts, and a strategy to generate steady local reviews. This increases visibility for 'near me' searches and map results, and combined with on-site SEO, improves chances of appearing in the local Map Pack (top 3)." },
